title:    Access follows membership, both ways
subtitle: Three trials each direction against the deployed group. The subject holds no role of its own.
width:    1120
---
$ ORG_ID=... ./scripts/measure-membership-lag.sh 3

Measuring membership propagation, 3 trial(s) each direction.
Subject: group-access-demo@...   Group: grp-gcp-log-readers@...
Poll 10s, ceiling 600s. A ceiling hit is reported, not retried.

--- trial 1 ---
  revoke: removing membership... access gone after 30s
  grant:  adding membership back... access back after 30s

--- trial 2 ---
  revoke: removing membership... access gone after 20s
  grant:  adding membership back... access back after 30s

--- trial 3 ---
  revoke: removing membership... access gone after 10s
  grant:  adding membership back... access back after 10s

== Result ==
  revoke   30,20,10s
  grant    30,30,10s
  [restore] membership put back

# The subject holds no role of its own. Every one of those six transitions
# is a membership change and nothing else - no IAM policy was edited.
